                <pb facs="0383" n="377" sameAs="frus:frus1901China/pg377"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hay to Mr. Rockhill.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1901-07-24"><hi rendition="#italic">July 24,
                        1901</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>(Mr. Hay states that payments in United States gold or in sterling at the rate of
                    four eighty-six sixty-five the pound will be equally satisfactory.</p>
                <p>Uniformity and least burden to China should be taken into consideration.)</p>
            </div>
        </body>
